Worked-example tests:

Artifact 1, Section 11.1 (uniform null, S2 support, W_adj, exactly solvable): the observed statistic should be 19.54, the exact exceedance probability should be 2.99 * 10^-3, and the simulator should produce an estimate consistent with the exact value within Monte Carlo error.

Artifact 1, Section 11.2 (what goes wrong if the support rule is ignored): the simulator with S1 support should produce a p-value of 1.37 * 10^-3, smaller than the correct S2 value.

Artifact 1, Section 11.3 (non-uniform null where the Lambda-maximizer is not the widest gap): the observed statistic should be 14.90 for the Lambda-maximizer, and the Monte Carlo reference should give p = 0.0167.

Artifact 1, Section 11.4 (small simulation of calibration and power): the false-positive rate at nominal 0.05 should be 0.051 for the full pipeline, and 0.086 for the fixed-support reference.

Artifact 1, Section 11.5 (nuisance estimation, gap-exclusion loop, and dependence): the full-pipeline reference should be within about two standard errors of nominal.

Artifact 1, Section 11.6 (pair windows, endpoint bias, endpoint-conditioned statistic): the critical values and power should match the reported values.

Artifact 1, Section 11.7 (selection function): the rejection rate should be 0.048 for the effective-null procedure and 0.204 for the procedure that omits selection.

